  "invariants": [
    "Existing classical wallets and rotating ML-DSA code 7 / profile 4 retain identity, derivation and wire bytes.",
    "Fixed ML-DSA code 8 / profile 5 binds account mode into its descriptor, permanent account ID and KDF; an existing account cannot switch modes.",
    "Fixed ML-DSA preserves its transaction public key and commitment while consuming each included authorization generation; failed dispatch and Shield sequencing retain replay protection.",
    "Rotating ML-DSA requires a nonzero, different next commitment; fixed ML-DSA requires the initial commitment as current and next.",
    "Both profiles retain the same post-quantum owner, delegate, protected-multisig, derivative, EVM and capability rules.",
    "Existing original dispatchables remain in use with unchanged deployed legacy call encodings; duplicate v2 dispatchables are absent.",
    "Both profiles retain signed-v4, the existing outer MultiSignature, a 5367-byte Raw proof and the same nonzero framing carrier.",
    "Finalized state supplies signing descriptor, generation and nonce; fixed signing rejects metadata without profile 5 before using private keys.",
    "Descriptor-bearing recipient addresses are preserved for registration; scheme and mode are restored from versioned keyfiles."
  ],
